he ordered pair $(x_1,x_2).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"120fdd95d77b85894ff2ea911f4f9a6fc1a7155c71c30e869d96d3f1555bb2d3"},"seconds":14.954715490341187,"seed":1152330740426481248,"stop":"eos","text":"Given the equations \\(x^3 + 5x^2 + px + q = 0\\) and \\(x^3 + 7x^2 + px + r = 0\\), let the common roots be \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). The third root of the first equation is \\(x_1\\) and the third root of the second equation is \\(x_2\\).\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, for the first equation \\(x^3 + 5x^2 + px + q = 0\\), we have:\n\\[\na + b + x_1 = -5 \\quad \\text{(1)}\n\\]\n\\[\nab + ax_1 + bx_1 = p \\quad \\text{(2)}\n\\]\n\\[\nabx_1 = -q \\quad \\text{(3)}\n\\]\n\nFor the second equation \\(x^3 + 7x^2 + px + r = 0\\), we have:\n\\[\na + b + x_2 = -7 \\quad \\text{(4)}\n\\]\n\\[\nab + ax_2 + bx_2 = p \\quad \\text{(5)}\n\\]\n\\[\nabx_2 = -r \\quad \\text{(6)}\n\\]\n\nFrom equations (1) and (4), we get:\n\\[\na + b + x_1 = -5 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad a + b + x_2 = -7\n\\]\nSubtracting these two equations, we obtain:\n\\[\nx_1 - x_2 = 2 \\quad \\text{(7)}\n\\]\n\nFrom equations (2) and (5), we get:\n\\[\nab + ax_1 + bx_1 = ab + ax_2 + bx_2\n\\]\nFactoring out the common terms, we have:\n\\[\na(x_1 - x_2) + b(x_1 - x_2) = 0\n\\]\nSince \\(x_1 \\neq x_2\\), we can factor out \\((x_1 - x_2)\\):\n\\[\n(x_1 - x_2)(a + b) = 0\n\\]\nSince \\(x_1 \\neq x_2\\), it follows that \\(a + b = 0\\). Substituting \\(a + b = 0\\) into equation (1), we get:\n\\[\n0 + x_1 = -5 \\implies x_1 = -5\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(a + b = 0\\) into equation (4), we get:\n\\[\n0 + x_2 = -7 \\implies x_2 = -7\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair \\((x_1, x_2)\\) is \\(\\boxed{(-5, -7)}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(-5, -7)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:829"}
